E. ChatGPT — Add custom MCP server
Name: Kivo CRM (or any label)
Description: Search CRM contacts via Kivo
Server URL: {PUBLIC_BASE_URL}/crm/mcp
Authentication: OAuth
Advanced OAuth registration: Predefined OAuth client (recommended for POC). Dynamic client registration is also enabled on the server if ChatGPT prefers DCR.
Callback URL: Shown in ChatGPT when you create/configure the connector — copy the exact HTTPS callback (often connection-specific). Do not guess.
OAuth client ID: Your chosen ID (e.g. chatgpt-crm) — must match CRM_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID in .env.
OAuth client secret: Leave empty if using a public client (token_endpoint_auth_method: none). Set only if you configure confidential client auth.
Token endpoint authentication: none (public client + PKCE) unless you set a secret and client_secret_post.
Scopes: crm:contacts:read
Next: Save, then complete OAuth when prompted (Company ID + CRM API Token on your login page).
Copy from ChatGPT → .env:

CRM_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URIS= exact callback URL(s), comma-separated if multiple
CRM_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID= (and secret if used)
Your .env must also include:

PUBLIC_BASE_URL = current ngrok HTTPS URL (no trailing slash)
BASE_URL = same URL (Weather)
CRM_OAUTH_JWT_SIGNING_KEY, CRM_CREDENTIAL_ENCRYPTION_KEY
